#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "70991204-370a-5804-a04e-7e664db052de" :question/math-academy-id "e-8048" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- $R_1 := \\ldots$\n\n- $R_3:=R_3-3R_2$\n\n- $R_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_2,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below $a_{22}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_1 := R_1 - 2R_2\\quad$ and $\\quad R_4:=R_4+2R_2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161690 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf8e85c-ffa6-55b9-a087-2a5272f10f25" :question/math-academy-id "e-8049" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- $C_1:=\\ldots$\n\n- $C_3:= C_3 - 4C_2$\n\n- $C_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_2,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{32}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 11 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+5C_2\\quad$ and $\\quad C_4:=C_4-2C_2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "399b7598-c793-5032-9f33-ac02c7b85fe1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8050" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_1,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below $a_{11}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_2:=R_2-2R_1\\quad$ and $\\quad R_3:=R_3+3R_1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f9912357-1d1d-5413-917e-257dc5dfc0fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-8051" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_3,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+6{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+5{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & -17 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+6C_3\\quad$ and $\\quad C_2:=C_2+5C_3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941c4e1-5e36-53ce-bc6b-7d6663d0963c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} + 4C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 3C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160525} {:answer/id #uuid "f458abd4-da18-5702-90a4-330e62adc6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160526} {:answer/id #uuid "1dabc275-1f78-58e5-af0a-2f8732ba71e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + 4C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160527} {:answer/id #uuid "34741622-1ae3-5eb4-ab55-84a7650c2729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 4C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160528} {:answer/id #uuid "5536cf5f-999a-5c38-9842-8c8dc2cc8268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 4C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 3C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34741622-1ae3-5eb4-ab55-84a7650c2729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 4C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160528} :answer-field/id #uuid "516f55fe-7fee-5a67-ba34-beb24397ddb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a68c2e7c-c605-5187-a1fa-13349acf01b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42917" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of ${a}_{33}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5422cf1-0456-5f5d-8ba6-3f1f5e16f0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305791} {:answer/id #uuid "9711bf45-ce56-5e08-b819-ad2eb5614771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305792} {:answer/id #uuid "a43bbb7c-3429-512f-8efe-aa259db83a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-9{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305793} {:answer/id #uuid "abd5d038-e4f3-5894-9d2f-c89114a0d5d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305794} {:answer/id #uuid "35661d74-55af-5ea3-959b-98ed00eec92c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abd5d038-e4f3-5894-9d2f-c89114a0d5d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305794} :answer-field/id #uuid "61171c50-503d-56c1-8580-ab358cf7bd75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec58f6f2-4cbf-5fb0-b33d-bce6328d302b" :question/math-academy-id "q-91160" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{13}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79fa33b-b535-5339-87f4-c6b4865abc9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-5{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305805} {:answer/id #uuid "8979b792-55e4-54c9-bfc5-98b9aaaa9d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305806} {:answer/id #uuid "895876d5-9a62-5b9e-b79a-8747e73ec064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305807} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec9085b-52d9-5ee4-80da-a96c3997f150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305808} {:answer/id #uuid "eb98513a-3da1-532e-8135-ec925695d2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb98513a-3da1-532e-8135-ec925695d2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-